Subject: [PATCH] feat: fleet error catalog v2 -- four risk tiers,
 operator_message for all 33 (v0.19.0) (#29)

Decided with the user 2026-09-18 (plan W1a). The five v1 tiers ordered
nothing a reader could use: R1 "propose, let a human decide" gave the
operator nothing to decide (the exchange is authoritative), R3's "auto-run
after a timeout unless a Telegram button is pressed" was never built, and
R2's after-the-fact notice reported bookkeeping that moved no money.

v2: R0 log / R1 auto, silent (was R2) / R2 auto-retry, escalate after
escalate_after=3 consecutive failures (was R1 + R3) / R3 human required
(was R4). audit_notice removed. Governance invariant unchanged in spirit:
MECHANICAL only in R0/R1, JUDGEMENT only in R2/R3.

- Catalog -> fleet-error-catalog-v2.json: every entry re-tiered; changed
  entries' auto_action/human_action/rationale rewritten (incl. two safety
  conditions before seykota auto-cancels an orphan stop); retired_codes lists
  MOM.VERIFIED_CLOSE_PROPOSED and SEY.VERIFIED_CLOSE_PROPOSED (emitted by
  seykota's shadow bot but never catalogued in v1).
- operator_message on all 33 entries (v1 had 3); R2/R3 also carry ai_prompt,
  a root-cause prompt to paste to an AI.
- RISK_TIERS four tiers; REQUESTABLE_TIERS = {R2, R3}; ops_export exports only
  R3 and escalated R2 (needs_human), appends the AI prompt with the event's
  code/id/evidence; fleet-ops-export v2. Event-log and request-queue schema
  enums follow.

No event log or request queue exists yet on either host (checked), so the
relabelling needs no data migration.

